Package: emeansR
Title: E-Means Clustering for Large Datasets
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Enrique", "Toledo", email = "enriquetoledo@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Authors of the bundled Rust crates", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "see inst/AUTHORS")
    )
Description: Implements e-means (Bessa et al. (2026) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2611.09501>),
    a mini-batch replacement for Lloyd's k-means that updates centroids with an
    exponential moving average and sets batch size and step size from fitted
    scaling laws, following the reference 'faiss' implementation. Reaches a
    lower loss than 25 Lloyd iterations in a few epochs. The compute core is
    written in 'Rust'.
